course: dictionary
lesson: 5858
title: What is a mammal?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mammal is an animal that has hair or fur, breathes air and feeds its babies with milk. Dogs, cats, cows, mice, whales, dolphins, bats and humans are all mammals.
explain: Mammals are warm-blooded, so they keep their bodies warm inside. «Snakes are cold-blooded, so they need far less food than mammals; a big python can go months without a meal.»
explain: Do not judge an animal by where it lives or how it moves. «Whales and dolphins live in the sea, but they are mammals.» Bats fly, and they are mammals too. The clues to look for are fur or hair, breathing air and milk for the babies.
fact: A mammal is an animal that has hair or fur, breathes air and feeds its babies with milk.
fact: Most mammals give birth to live babies instead of laying eggs.
fact: A few mammals, such as the platypus and echidna of Australia, lay eggs.
fact: «All mammals feed their babies with milk made in the mother's body, so every baby mammal needs its mother at the start of its life.»
fact: «Spotted hyenas have some of the strongest bites of any mammal.»
exercise: «Snakes are cold-blooded, so they need far less food than mammals.» Which animal in this list is a mammal? | Salmon | Snake | Shark | *Bat
exercise: «Whales and dolphins live in the sea, but they are mammals.» What is a clue that a whale is a mammal? | It is very big | It has a fin | It lives in the sea | *It breathes air and feeds its babies with milk
exercise: «All mammals feed their babies with milk made in the mother's body.» What do mammals feed their babies with? | Seeds | *Milk | Water | Insects
test: Which of these is NOT a mammal? | Human | *Snake | Dog | Whale
test: Most mammals do what with their babies? | *Give birth to live babies | Feed them with seeds | Hatch them from eggs | Leave them in a nest
exam: Which fact is true of the platypus, a mammal from Australia? | *It lays eggs | It has no hair | It lives only on land | It has feathers
